import equational_theories.Definability.CloneExtra4

/-!
# A clone of two hundred and fifty-eight

Five times the size of any family in `CloneExtra.lean` through `CloneExtra4.lean`, and the reason
it is possible at all is the representation. Both the family and its composition table are
`Array (Array Nat)` rather than nested `![...]` vectors, and for the family that is not a
convenience but the difference between three minutes and an hour: `![...]` is a chain of
`Matrix.cons`, so reaching member `i` costs `i` steps, and the composition check reaches every
member for every pair of members, paying that cost cubed. An array is indexed in one step.

The shape of the literals matters too. A flat array of sixty-six thousand entries overruns the
recursion limit while it is being built, and sixty-six thousand nested `Matrix.cons` applications
is a term the elaborator does not finish; two hundred and fifty-eight rows of two hundred and
fifty-eight entries is neither. The checks are `native_decide` rather than `decide!`, since the
composition law alone is a million evaluations.

This file is generated by `genclone5.py`.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 8000

open Law Law.MagmaLaw

namespace Magma

